{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,30]],"date-time":"2026-07-30T11:10:02Z","timestamp":1785409802079,"version":"3.56.0"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,13]]},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"American Chemical Society (ACS)","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,13]],"date-time":"2025-05-13T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1747094400000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100000781","name":"European Research Council","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["101076997"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["101076997"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100000781","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/100004412","name":"Human Frontier Science Program","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["RGP003\/2023"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["RGP003\/2023"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100004412","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001659","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["CRC 392"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["CRC 392"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001659","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":[],"abstract":"<jats:p>RNA droplets assembled from co-transcriptionally folded nanostructures have recently emerged as a promising platform for constructing protocells and minimal synthetic cell models. In these systems, a custom-designed DNA template encodes an RNA nanostar, which is produced by transcription and self-assembles into droplets by kissing-loop interactions. Here, we show that such RNA droplets encapsulate their own DNA template, creating a genotype-phenotype link as the key prerequisite for evolution. We find that low mutation rates in the DNA template increase the phenotypical and functional complexity of the RNA droplets - enabling stable vacuole formation. With reverse-engineering and next-generation sequencing, we identify specific nanostar architectures that act as surfactants and are responsible for this morphological transition. Strikingly, vacuolated droplets exhibit micrometer-scale movement driven by internal vacuole dynamics, leading to enhanced fusion and growth - an emergent functional phenotype that results from mutagenesis. Our findings establish RNA droplets as self-contained, evolvable systems, opening new avenues for the bottom-up evolution of synthetic cells and origins-of-life research.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.26434\/chemrxiv-2025-5ffnn","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,14]],"date-time":"2025-05-14T00:56:17Z","timestamp":1747184177000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["Genetic encoding and mutagenesis of RNA droplet phenotypes"],"prefix":"10.26434","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0005-4458-9579","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"William","family":"Verstraeten","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/04rcqnp59","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"Heidelberg University","place":["United States"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Mai P.","family":"Tran","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/04rcqnp59","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"Heidelberg University","place":["United States"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Alena","family":"Taskina","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/04rcqnp59","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"Heidelberg University","place":["United States"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0002-1309-6585","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Moritz","family":"Hamberger","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https